OL,3,GNEWSAPolice phone number spoofed to
OL,4,Ascam victims
OL,5,
OL,6,FFraudsters have been spoofing police
OL,7,Fphone numbers to call unsuspecting
OL,8,Fvictims and trick them into
OL,9,Ftransferring money to them, detectives
OL,10,Fsay.
OL,12,FMerseyside Police said one victim
OL,13,Ftransferred what the force said was a
OL,14,Fsignificant amount of money.
OL,16,FThe force said the criminals pretended
OL,17,Fto be detectives investigating identity
OL,18,Fthefts in order to get people to give
OL,19,Fthem their bank details or information
OL,20,Fabout any cryptocurrency they might
OL,21,Fhave.
